text.section:
In addition, the Commissioner may cancel the license, permit or registration of any person who willfully fails to comply with this chapter by:

Failing to file the tonnage report;


Falsifying information;


Making an inaccurate statement of tonnage distributed in the Commonwealth during any reporting year;


Making an inaccurate listing of regulated products for registration;


Failing to pay the license, permit, registration or inspection fee;


Failing to accurately report any of the information required to be submitted under this chapter;


Failing to keep records for a period of three years; or


Failing to allow inspection of records by the Commissioner.
